Build succeeds. Here's the pattern I implemented:

## Architecture

| Requirement | Solution |
|---|---|
| App-wide read/write | **Scoped `ThemeState` service** with `Action OnChange` event |
| Cross–render-mode updates | `ThemeIndicator` in layout uses `@rendermode InteractiveServer` (interactive island) |
| Per-user isolation | `AddScoped` → one instance per circuit |
| Persists across nav | Circuit survives enhanced navigation; scoped service lives with it |
| Immediate updates | All subscribers call `StateHasChanged` via `OnChange` event |

### Key insight

A `<CascadingValue>` in your static layout **cannot** reach interactive children. Instead:

1. **`ThemeState`** (scoped service) — any interactive component injects it, reads/writes freely, subscribes to `OnChange`.
2. **`ThemeIndicator`** — an interactive island (`@rendermode InteractiveServer`) embedded in the static layout. Because it's interactive, it shares the same circuit and `ThemeState` instance as your pages.
3. **Settings page** — changes `ThemeState`, which fires `OnChange`, instantly updating the header indicator and any other subscriber.

To consume the theme from any other interactive component, just:

```razor
@inject ThemeState Theme
@implements IDisposable

@code {
    protected override void OnInitialized() => Theme.OnChange += StateHasChanged;
    public void Dispose() => Theme.OnChange -= StateHasChanged;
}
```
